cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "lexindex: compact, immutable string-to-id indexes for huge catalogs"
abstract: >-
  Compact, immutable string-to-id indexes for huge catalogs, with a Rust core and
  Python bindings. Three complementary build-once / query-many structures: an ordered
  FST-backed index with prefix, range, fuzzy (Levenshtein) and subsequence queries; a
  minimal-perfect-hash dictionary with verified membership and reverse lookup; and a
  fingerprint-based minimal-perfect-hash map storing no keys at all (~1.3 bytes/key on
  real dictionary words). All serialise to flat, memory-mappable blobs.
authors:
